Mr. Hamilton, could you please share with us this particular donation?

931
00:59:41,540 --> 00:59:48,700
So Council is familiar with the area up on Green Mountain that is obviously well inside

932
00:59:48,700 --> 00:59:52,980
of our city but somewhat remote just based on the terrain.

933
00:59:52,980 --> 00:59:58,220
It does have fire coverage from one of our career fire stations down at the bottom of

934
00:59:58,220 --> 00:59:59,220
the mountain.

935
00:59:59,220 --> 01:00:03,500
But that community for many, many years has also resourced a volunteer fire department

936
01:00:03,500 --> 01:00:08,020
that assists with emergency response up on the mountain.

937
01:00:08,020 --> 01:00:14,180
In recent years we've worked more closely with them, have actually provided some real

938
01:00:14,180 --> 01:00:20,100
estate while they really provided it to us and then we allow them to use the small fire

939
01:00:20,100 --> 01:00:23,180
units up there but also have assisted them with the equipment.

940
01:00:23,180 --> 01:00:27,060
So one of the trucks that they have right now is one that we actually provided to them

941
01:00:27,060 --> 01:00:31,740
out of our fire department and it's now time to replace that.

942
01:00:31,740 --> 01:00:35,260
We think the arrangement there and then ultimately there is a point in the future where we will

943
01:00:35,260 --> 01:00:39,740
need to build a permanent fire station up on the mountain.

944
01:00:39,740 --> 01:00:42,600
So we've identified the piece of equipment they need.

945
01:00:42,600 --> 01:00:47,460
They did some fundraising and now want to donate that money, about $110,000, to the

946
01:00:47,460 --> 01:00:50,740
community to contribute towards the purchase of the truck that they'll use.

947
01:00:50,740 --> 01:00:54,780
So ultimately between this and then what we have in our fleet capital account already

948
01:00:54,780 --> 01:00:58,500
in the capital plan, we will purchase the equipment and then provide that to them to

949
01:00:58,500 --> 01:01:01,220
use for emergency response up on the mountain.

950
01:01:01,220 --> 01:01:06,800
And this truck is unique in that it has the capacity to take water far beyond what they

951
01:01:06,800 --> 01:01:08,380
could get from a hydrant.

952
01:01:08,380 --> 01:01:11,220
There's really kind of two issues that we have to deal with up there on the mountain.

953
01:01:11,220 --> 01:01:15,580
There's a portion of the development there that are very, very large lots, multiple acres.

954
01:01:15,580 --> 01:01:19,860
In many cases the houses are well off of the public right of way.

955
01:01:19,860 --> 01:01:24,860
So we have to deal with much longer runs of lines to get water into the house if there's

956
01:01:24,860 --> 01:01:26,060
a fire there.

957
01:01:26,060 --> 01:01:29,620
We also have sometimes incidents of wildland fires there.

958
01:01:29,620 --> 01:01:33,820
So dealing with grass fires and unbrushed fire, things like that.

959
01:01:33,820 --> 01:01:37,660
And so this equipment is a little bit smaller and actually more maneuverable to get into

960
01:01:37,660 --> 01:01:41,060
some of those driveways and things over those long distances as well as helping with the

961
01:01:41,060 --> 01:01:42,660
wildland fire.

962
01:01:42,660 --> 01:01:47,180
And I should also add for the record that at the next council meeting we will see I'm

